  "texts": {
    "preamble": "G.S.Brown vs Attingal Muncipality on 8 June, 2015",
    "facts": "EXHIBIT P6 TRUE COPY OF THE COMPLAINT SUBMITTED BY THE PETITIONER BEFORE THE SUB INSPECTOR OF POLICE, ATTINGAL, DATED 3.8.2016. The petitioner has approached this Court aggrieved by Ext.P5 notice that was served on him, seeking his explanation in respect of certain food items that were seized from his premises which were alleged to be of inferior quality. While the petitioner submitted his objections to Ext.P5 notice, during the pendency of the writ petition, Ext.P7 notice was issued to the petitioner by the 2nd respondent, proposing a cancellation of his licence [D & O licence]. It is submitted that, to Ext.P7 notice, the petitioner has preferred Ext.P8 reply before the 2nd respondent, and no orders have been passed thereon. While so, by Ext.P9 notice, the petitioner was also informed that, on account of the pendency of this writ petition as also the non-finalisation of proceedings, pursuant to Ext.P7 notice, his application for renewal of the licence for the year 2017-18 could not be considered by the respondents. The petitioner further submits that, against Ext.P9 notice, the petitioner has preferred Ext.P10 appeal and Ext.P11 stay petition before the Tribunal for Local Self Government Institutions. On a consideration of the facts and circumstances of the case as also the submissions made across the bar, I find that Ext.P5 notice, that was impugned in the writ petition, initially, was only in the nature of a show cause notice, to which, the petitioner has admittedly submitted a reply [Ext.P6]. Thereafter, during the pendency of the writ petition, the petitioner was served with Ext.P7 notice, which, again, is in the nature of a show cause notice proposing a cancellation of the licence granted to the petitioner under the Kerala Municipality Act. The petitioner was also served with Ext.P9 notice, which indicated that his application for renewal of D & O licence could not be considered for the ensuing year, on account of the pendency of the earlier mentioned proceedings.",
    "arguments": "",
